# .env.test.example - Template for integration test configuration
#
# Copy this file to .env.test and fill in your test credentials:
#   cp .env.test.example .env.test
#
# IMPORTANT: .env.test is gitignored to protect credentials
#
# ===== GITHUB TEST ENVIRONMENT SETUP =====
#
# Option 1: Use Your Personal Account (Quick Start)
# ------------------------------------------------
# Pros: Easy, no setup needed
# Cons: Creates projects in your personal account
#
# 1. Use your GitHub username for TRACKER_GITHUB_ORGANIZATION
# 2. Tests will create/delete projects in your personal account
# 3. Project names include timestamp: "Migration Agent Test - {username} - {timestamp}"
#
# Option 2: Create a Test Organization (Recommended)
# ---------------------------------------------------
# Pros: Isolated testing, clean separation from personal/work projects
# Cons: Requires GitHub organization (free tier available)
#
# 1. Create a test organization at https://github.com/organizations/new
#    - Name: e.g., "my-username-testing" or "migration-agent-test"
#    - Plan: Free (for public projects)
# 2. Enable GitHub Projects in organization settings
# 3. Use organization name for TRACKER_GITHUB_ORGANIZATION
#
# Setup Instructions:
# 1. Choose Option 1 (personal) or Option 2 (organization) above
# 2. Create a GitHub Personal Access Token with 'project' and 'repo' scopes
#    at https://github.com/settings/tokens
# 3. Copy this file to .env.test
# 4. Replace the values below with your test credentials
# 5. Run integration tests: make test-integration

# ===== GitHub Tracker Configuration =====
# Required for GitHub integration tests

# GitHub Personal Access Token with 'project' scope
# Get token at: https://github.com/settings/tokens
TRACKER_GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your_token_here

# GitHub organization or username for testing
# Tests will create temporary projects in this organization
TRACKER_GITHUB_ORGANIZATION=your-org-or-username

# REQUIRED: Project name for integration tests
# Integration tests require an explicit project name to improve test clarity
# and make test projects easily identifiable in GitHub UI.
# Replace this example value with your own project name.
TRACKER_GITHUB_PROJECT_NAME=My Integration Test Project

# ===== Optional Configuration =====

# (Optional) Existing project number to test with
# If not specified, tests will auto-create a temporary project
# WARNING: Setting this will modify an existing project!
# TRACKER_GITHUB_PROJECT_NUMBER=5

# (Optional) Project description for test projects
# Only used when creating new projects (not for existing project_number)
# TRACKER_GITHUB_PROJECT_DESCRIPTION=Integration test project for tracker functionality

# ===== Test Behavior Configuration =====

# Whether to keep test projects after tests complete
# Useful for debugging failed tests
# Default: false (cleanup runs automatically)
# TEST_KEEP_PROJECT=false

# Minimum GitHub API rate limit to run tests
# Tests will skip if rate limit is below this value
# Default: 20
# TEST_MIN_RATE_LIMIT=20
